  <event id="21">
      <start>11:00</start>
      <duration>01:00</duration>
      <room>AW1.125</room>
      <slug></slug>
      <title>Secret debian internals</title>
      <subtitle></subtitle>
      <track>Debian</track>
      <type></type>
      <language></language>
      <abstract>&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Debian is full of nice undocumented pieces of infrastructure: you can access control files of all source packages, aggregated package lists, popcon results, raw BTS data, Debtags categories, maintainer/comaintainer databases, build logs and much more.&#xA;&lt;/p&gt;&#xA; </abstract>
      <description>&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Since it&amp;#39;s usually hard to find documentation on what is available and on how to use it, I&amp;#39;ll show you what I know. People from the audience can show some more. Hopefully someone will blog a summary on Planet Debian.&#xA;&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Then we hack.&#xA;&lt;/p&gt;&#xA; </description>
      <persons>
          <person id="211">Enrico Zini</person>
      </persons>
